    "created_at": "2017-03-06T08:10:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-06T08:10:44Z",
    "body": "@domenic: Yes. I think it makes sense to use the `integrity` attribute to govern the content of the top-level fetch, and to rely on an as-yet-to-be-invented mechanism for integrity checks on branch-level fetches.\r\n\r\nWith regard to `require-sri-for`, yes, those internal branch requests would fail. That's an argument for y'all to get to work on SRI2, I think. :)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
